    {
        "content": "<p>Hi all, I used Claude to draft a proof of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cantelli%27s_inequality\">Cantelli's inequality</a> which seemed like a good starting point for a contribution since the result is pretty self-contained. However, I recognize that the <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/contribute/index.html\">Contributing to mathlib</a> page recommends engaging with the community on Zulip before making a PR that has AI-generated code.</p>\n<p>I iterated with Claude to simplify the proof, and checked that it builds locally. I understand the high level proof strategy and what each line does, but might not grasp all the nuances. The change can be viewed at my fork <a href=\"https://github.com/blfang/mathlib4/commit/da71879da66a45ef3cf269c719a1b315eb278634\">here</a>; it is added next to Chebychev's inequality, also pasted below. Would appreciate any feedback on whether this is appropriate for mathlib4 or if the proof needs improvement. Thanks!</p>\n<div class=\"spoiler-block\"><div class=\"spoiler-header\">\n</div><div class=\"spoiler-content\" aria-hidden=\"true\">\n<div class=\"codehilite\"><pre><span></span><code>/-- **Cantelli's inequality**, also known as the one-sided Chebyshev inequality: the probability\nthat a real random variable exceeds its expectation by at least `c &gt; 0` is at most\n`Var[X] / (Var[X] + c ^ 2)`. -/\ntheorem meas_sub_integral_ge_le_variance_div [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] {X : Ω → ℝ}\n    (hX : MemLp X 2 μ) {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 &lt; c) :\n    μ {ω | c ≤ X ω - μ[X]} ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (Var[X; μ] / (Var[X; μ] + c ^ 2)) := by\n  have hu : 0 ≤ Var[X; μ] / c := div_nonneg (variance_nonneg X μ) hc.le\n  set u := Var[X; μ] / c\n  have hXi := hX.integrable one_le_two\n  have hW : MemLp (fun ω ↦ X ω - μ[X] + u) 2 μ := (hX.sub (memLp_const _)).add (memLp_const _)\n  -- The second moment of `X - 𝔼[X] + u` is `Var[X] + u ^ 2`.\n  have h := variance_eq_sub hW\n  rw [variance_add_const (by fun_prop), variance_sub_const (by fun_prop),\n    integral_add (by fun_prop) (integrable_const _), integral_sub hXi (integrable_const _)] at h\n  simp only [Pi.pow_apply, integral_const, probReal_univ, one_smul, sub_self, zero_add] at h\n  -- Markov's inequality applied to `(X - 𝔼[X] + u) ^ 2`.\n  have := mul_meas_ge_le_integral_of_nonneg (.of_forall fun _ ↦ sq_nonneg _) hW.integrable_sq\n    ((c + u) ^ 2)\n  calc μ {ω | c ≤ X ω - μ[X]}\n    _ ≤ μ {ω | (c + u) ^ 2 ≤ (X ω - μ[X] + u) ^ 2} :=\n      measure_mono fun ω (hω : c ≤ _) ↦ show (c + u) ^ 2 ≤ _ by gcongr\n    _ ≤ ENNReal.ofReal ((Var[X; μ] + u ^ 2) / (c + u) ^ 2) := by\n      rw [← ofReal_measureReal]\n      exact ENNReal.ofReal_le_ofReal &lt;| by rw [le_div_iff₀ (by positivity)]; linarith\n    _ = ENNReal.ofReal (Var[X; μ] / (Var[X; μ] + c ^ 2)) := by\n      congr 1\n      simp only [u]\n      field_simp\n      ring\n\n/-- **Cantelli's inequality** for the lower tail: the probability that a real random variable is\nbelow its expectation by at least `c &gt; 0` is at most `Var[X] / (Var[X] + c ^ 2)`. -/\ntheorem meas_integral_sub_ge_le_variance_div [IsProbabilityMeasure μ] {X : Ω → ℝ}\n    (hX : MemLp X 2 μ) {c : ℝ} (hc : 0 &lt; c) :\n    μ {ω | c ≤ μ[X] - X ω} ≤ ENNReal.ofReal (Var[X; μ] / (Var[X; μ] + c ^ 2)) := by\n  simpa [integral_neg, variance_fun_neg, neg_add_eq_sub] using\n    meas_sub_integral_ge_le_variance_div (X := fun ω ↦ -X ω) hX.neg hc\n</code></pre></div>\n</div></div>",
        "id": 628204004,
        "sender_full_name": "blfang",
        "timestamp": 1790803649
