    {
        "content": "<p>Could you please first clarify what your goals are with this?</p>",
        "id": 628224322,
        "sender_full_name": "Snir Broshi",
        "timestamp": 1790811797
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>At a high level I'd like to add more results from undergrad probability/stats that aren't in mathlib yet, and in the process become more familiar with mathlib and Lean.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>I saw a result about the variance of the binomial distribution in <code>Wanted/Probability</code>, but there seems to already be a PR for that.</li>\n<li>I'd like to add results about Poisson processes, but it seems like I'd need to build up theory about counting processes in general, which probably is a bigger task, and not a good idea for a first PR.</li>\n<li>Cantelli's inequality seemed self-contained enough that it could be a simple first PR. But perhaps I am misguided?...</li>\n</ul>",
        "id": 628225920,
        "sender_full_name": "blfang",
        "timestamp": 1790812590
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>fwiw I've played the Natural Number Game and other games on the Lean Game Server (without the use of AI), and I've read part of Mathematics in Lean, but it seems this is not sufficient to contribute to mathlib? what else do I need to do? are there other tasks that are more appropriate for contributing in the probability/stats space?</p>",
        "id": 628226501,
        "sender_full_name": "blfang",
        "timestamp": 1790812857
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"708362\">blfang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Probability.3A.20Cantelli.27s.20inequality.20draft/near/628225920\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>become more familiar with mathlib and Lean</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>How does Claude writing code you said you don't fully grasp help with this goal?</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"708362\">blfang</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Probability.3A.20Cantelli.27s.20inequality.20draft/near/628226501\">said</a>:</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>it seems this is not sufficient to contribute to mathlib</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>It probably depends on which parts of MIL, but do you have specific questions that we could help you with?<br>\nFor example have you tried proving Cantelli yourself and struggled? What issues have you run into?<br>\nHave you read <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/blog/posts/basic-probability-in-mathlib/\">Basic probability in Mathlib</a>?</p>",
